  "aqg_implication": "G1 is supported on the consensus items. Gap labels carry human-aligned signal, so conditioning a question pool on the gap matrix is a defensible personalization step. The hybrid score separates the human binary, but it does not beat every single signal under the CI rule. Keep the hybrid as the production score. Do not claim it dominates TF-IDF, BM25, and semantic similarity. On the consensus subset, 12 of 17 system-gap items were judged met or partial (0 with no stored evidence string, 12 with a stored neighbor). The requirement phrase is a literal substring of the CV in 0 of those false gaps. A stored neighbor that is a different competency, plus an absent phrase, is not the same failure as finding the right evidence and scoring it low. The 6-item count is also not a population rate, because items without rater consensus are excluded. G4 does not adopt a new configuration. Production weights 0.25/0.25/0.50 and thresholds 0.65/0.40/0.20 stay. The next gain in question quality is selection balance on the pools already generated, not another threshold search on these items.",
  "note": "Consensus drops items the two assigned annotators did not agree on, unless adjudicated.csv resolves them. G4 adoption uses primary-30 to choose a configuration and holdout-30 to test it.",
